ough would that be  you either get it to em beat or let Ben  Simmons take it right yeah yes you know  it's at times it's not much more  complicated than that okay but let's go  back because people forget what you went  through and we had you on during this  process did you ever have one of those  or the last time you had one of those  moments where you just you know what it  got to you where you just said I I just  don't know if I'm gonna see the light at  the end of the tunnel I mean during the  ten win season and you know you lost 26  in a row and we had multiple injuries  and we really haven't had much good  fortune here in Philadelphia without  first draft picks either playing at all  for an entire season or staying healthy  for the large majority of it I think  during that period of time you know you  wanted did you you know times was it  something that you thought you were  signing up for and we all sort of have a  coaching mortality on the son of a coach  and so you recognize you know the  industry and you know yes to your  question of course and I did feel  comfortable and confident we were  working on the correct things my version  of what I think a culture is when it  would it wouldn't wouldn't reflect like  winning and losing which is what  everybody sort of looks at you know what  times you you you would you know have  some late nights but when the last time  I spoke with you compared to where we  are now that seems like a long time ago  you went from ten to fifty two wins in  two years I mean that's pretty terrible  there did you ever worry did you ever  think you were getting fired oh yeah you  know you always thought about it like I  I think the relationship that I had with  with the owners in regards to what the  plan was like they brought me into New  York City five years ago  and they said this is a wish you know  how do we rebuild a culture how do we  start from Ground Zero and rebuild it  and at that stage for me I was what  fifty three years old