k you  do know I think I think everybody  searches for like this clandestine you  know conspiracy theory and it's clear he  was injured and he his shot you know  took a hit I'm sure there were times  that he was aware of that in his mind  he's the first player chosen you know  Philadelphia isn't sort of a you know  warm and fuzzy marketplace and I think  it's just like human nature exacerbated  by a injury to a shoulder and the good  news is out of all the years that I've  been coached and I've been doing this a  long time did this this this the human  side of this story is is incredibly  endearing to me he's a remarkable person  you know like you want to hug him as  much as you want to coach him he's just  really good people and so to fast  forward like and go through all this  stuff he went through and now he's  playing NBA basketball in his last you  know game he had a triple-double the  youngest in the history of the NBA  like those are the memories stand that I  would like to marketplace to hear and  and that's the truth you know like  that's all the whole thing sort of  unfolded yeah I felt bad for him at this  video almost like surveillance video of  his shot and then it came out and then I  was saying gosh I just hope you guys  shut him down so he's not subjected to  this because it felt like he lost  confidence in that shot and you can even  watch him as great as he is to get a  triple-double I'm still looking at do  defenses respect that jump shot right  now and they probably don't and you know  that's all fear you know I hear you and  I think that's all fear and so be it  it's uh and the NBA playoffs are so  incredibly different in the regular  season to beat somebody four times and  you know have to game plan each game  gets a little bit more granular in the  secrets become less and less and so you  know the judgment of how they guard mark  Kellogg  you know we're gonna see some stuff it's  different than rolling into a city you  know an 82-game regular 